<title>USA: CBOT Sept volume rises 1.5 percent year-on-year.</title>
<headline>CBOT Sept volume rises 1.5 percent year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade (CBOT) said its futures and options volume totalled 17,401,625 contracts in September, up 1.5 percent from 17,137,050 contracts in September 1995.</p>
<p>CBOT added that volume in the first nine months of 1996 had risen 5.9 percent to 170,487,642 contracts from 161,026,010 contracts in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Volume in major categories and in selected individual contracts is as follows, with volume for September and percentage change followed by September 1995 volume:</p>
<p>All futures     13,449,539     - 1.7     13,680,707</p>
<p>  Agricultural   3,524,118     + 7.2	3,288,566</p>
<p>  Financial	9,922,075     - 4.5     10,387,518</p>
<p>All options on</p>
<p>	 futures   3,952,086     +14.3	3,456,343</p>
<p>  Agricultural   1,158,319     +31.7	  879,758</p>
<p>  Financial	2,789,542     + 8.3	2,575,909</p>
<p>Futures (individual)</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     6,926,086     - 5.3	7,317,138</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes 1,810,371     - 2.6	1,859,001</p>
<p>  US 5-yr notes    979,020     - 2.9	1,008,739</p>
<p>  Wheat		305,448     -30.0	  436,145</p>
<p>  Corn	     1,183,440     - 3.0	1,220,222</p>
<p>  Soybeans	 1,050,186     +31.2	  800,238</p>
<p>  Soymeal	    520,525     + 8.0	  481,949</p>
<p>  Soyoil	     425,850     +40.1	  303,893</p>
<p>Options</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     2,047,634     + 8.5	1,887,499</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes   499,571     + 9.5	  456,205</p>
<p>  Corn		 489,552     +36.6	  358,302</p>
<p>  Soybeans	   496,912     +45.7	  341,148</p>
<p>-- Chicago Derivatives Desk (312) 408 8750</p>
